text:
@khan9503-e7e Never said the stock market is the one and only hedge against inflation — but it is one of the best places to house your money in today’s market. Equities are real businesses that can raise prices while USD get torched daily (exactly what you mentioned).

K-shaped economy: where do you think the top half of that K’s wealth actually is? It’s overwhelmingly parked in the US stock market. In a market-cap weighted basket you’re barely holding the dying bottom half; you’re riding the winners pulling the whole K upward. That’s effectively the point. I’m not pro. K economy but we are too far gone imo and you are doing yourself and your family a massive disservice not to buy in. 

There’s no blind hope. I’m betting on the side that holds the real wealth and pricing power. history shows that side wins far more often than the hard-asset crowd wants to admit in 2026. And to be clear, i hold gold and silver, just not in a meaningful allocation.

@huruukko9419 even if you avoid a crash your cash grows at a slower rate than inflation usually. 

Also if the market doesn’t crash, the version of you that stayed in the market would be well ahead of you in gains

If you want the least risk and the most return you should dollar cost average your money into a 80/20 portfolio of total market index funds like VT and BNDW. It’s very easy to set up and you can get that money out tax free using a Roth IRA

@Cienfuegotv No it has not. 18 Trillion USD in total movement. Tax Cut number of 8 Trillion plus roughly 6 Trillion from Tax Revenue plus 4 Trillion from The Deficit makes it 18 Trillion total. 

18k points in a subtraction off the DOW but then either 4.6T or 5.3T in resettlement at the end. 6 weeks for a temporary crash then 2 weeks for resettlement. Number at the end of the market adjustment/correction will line up with the National Debt number. The math was already spoken about back in 2020. When you add money, you already know where it goes on the long position.

Aggressive Growth stocks will pop off b/c that's how it works. Over the cycle the bear sleeps while the Tax Cut gets pumped into the market. Soon as all that money gets depleted into the market, the bull runs. Inflationary bubble pops. Market offsets. Then they add more money aka next "Tax Cut" number of 12 Trillion.
